  <section|Reorganized proofs and exact conventions><label|reorganized-proofs-and-exact-conventions>

  <\itemize-dot>
    <item>Injectivity of E_t is proved by repeated halving and strong
    continuity, a valid shorter variant of the source's analytic
    identity-theorem proof. The imaginary unitary group is still constructed
    on the dense range of E_1. Spectral zero is never assigned an imaginary
    power by continuous calculus.

    <item>Complex duration is <verbatim|-i z - p> on the initial vector leg
    and <verbatim|-i(z_j-z_i)-2p> between insertions. Real-time translation
    has sign +i in its spectral exponent.

    <item>The independent-height Gram path is (-n s,...,-s,t,...,m t). The
    first real position tuple is reversed but NOT geometrically reflected.
    The first labels and tests are reversed and starred/conjugated.

    <item>Joint tempered boundary uses the exact finite Taylor formula on
    weakly ordered heights. It is stronger than fixed-profile convergence and
    applies to arbitrary ratios of the two independent heat parameters.

    <item>Fourier convention: test transform integrates exp(-i X.p), with
    inverse factor (2 pi)^(-4n); the distribution transform is W composed
    with that same hat. The halfspace result concerns absolute-coordinate
    momenta and all suffix sums.

    <item>The field common domain is the finite span of all word vectors. Its
    null space is invariant because of the star-concatenation pairing
    identity, not because positivity alone makes arbitrary concatenation
    bounded. No field boundedness or essential self-adjointness is claimed.
  </itemize-dot>

  <section|Literature><label|literature>

  The continuous calculus uses the already inspected Williams, Theorem 2.19,
  printed p.34, in its bounded self-adjoint specialization. The calculus
  input is separate from the explicitly proved complex heat and edge
  construction. See phase-evidence.md for bibliographic URL and source
  verification. There is no invocation of a blanket OS reconstruction theorem
  in these new chapters.

  <section|Remaining inputs after these chapters><label|remaining-inputs-after-these-chapters>

  The actual all-copy slab bound, finite-level inclusions, Euclidean
  hierarchy and reflection involution still depend on earlier construction
  work. Conditional on those inputs, complex heat, strict-time analytic
  matrices, joint tempered boundary, heat-vector positivity and translation
  embedding are now supplied. The following remain substantive: actual
  Lorentz label representation; spacelike locality; actual RG/UV estimates
  and OPE/trace outputs. The field reconstruction theorem deliberately
  displays these hypotheses where used.

  <section|Lorentz continuation and an alternative boundary-detection
  proof><label|lorentz-continuation-and-an-alternative-boundary-detection-proof>

  <verbatim|lorentz-covariance.tex> follows inspected C07/Euclid, Geometry,
  Integrate, Continue; C08; C09; and Work/A16. Exact declarations include
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C07.oriented_differential>, <verbatim|orbit_image>,
  <verbatim|error_imag>, <verbatim|compact_boost>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C08.answer>, <verbatim|YM.Work.C09.boost_corner>,
  <verbatim|moving_eval>, <verbatim|boost_invariant>, <verbatim|answer>, and
  <verbatim|YM.Work.A16.exists_rest>, <verbatim|answer>. It proves tested
  Ward transport, strong Schwartz pullback, integration along boosts, and
  finite generation of the proper orthochronous group. It still assumes the
  actual compatible finite-level Lorentz label action with derivative -i
  times the Euclidean plane generator.

  <verbatim|boundary-detection.tex> proves tensor density by the compact
  Fourier-cutoff/ Schwartz-quadrature method of inspected
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C25.cut_port_mem>, <verbatim|compact_mem>,
  <verbatim|answer>; supplies the <verbatim|Symbol> and <verbatim|Cam> inputs
  of <verbatim|YM.Work.C29.answer>; and follows
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C26.marker_on_joint>, <verbatim|strict_zero>,
  <verbatim|read_zero>, <verbatim|answer>. After tensor density gives zero
  joint W, the linear definition of tube emission makes that emission zero;
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.Surface.Aurora.lower> in Shift/Sol uses FullBody.pure
  to obtain zero strict-time values. Sorting and Conf continuity then give
  the Euclidean null criterion. The initial independent shorter
  frequency-testing route was removed following the user's main-step-fidelity
  clarification. The current chapter uses the actual C26 main construction.

  R. B. Melrose, <em|Introduction to Microlocal Analysis>, Chapter1, Ÿ1.7,
  Theorem1.3, printed p.22, equations(1.59)\U(1.61) printed p.21, author PDF
  <hlink|https://math.mit.edu/~rbm/iml/Chapter1.pdf|https://math.mit.edu/~rbm/iml/Chapter1.pdf>,
  actually inspected via web reader. Fourier transform is a continuous
  isomorphism of Schwartz space with inverse factor(2pi)^(-d), exactly the
  radian convention here. This background supplies Fourier
  inversion/homeomorphism only; the tensor-density quadrature and
  boundary-detection arguments are given in full in the manuscript.

  <section|Joint momentum and reconciliation with the new
  blueprint><label|joint-momentum-and-reconciliation-with-the-new-blueprint>

  <verbatim|spectral-measure.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|YM.Paley.same>, <verbatim|bound>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Paley/Line.lean>), <verbatim|YM.Paley.smoothed>,
  <verbatim|supports> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Paley/Half.lean>),
  <verbatim|YM.OS.Semigroup.altitude>, <verbatim|nonneg>
  (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Heat/Lift.lean>), and
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.Action.placed>, <verbatim|south>,
  <verbatim|spectrum>, <verbatim|only> (<verbatim|Lean/YM/Fields/Spectrum.lean>).
  The manuscript proves the Gaussian shift, support positivity,
  characteristic-function uniqueness, Lorentz improvement, projection
  identity and vacuum uniqueness. It cites SNAG in place of reproducing
  <verbatim|YM.Spectral.Orbit.P> / <verbatim|total> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/SNAG/Escape.lean>.

  B. Bekka, P. de la Harpe and A. Valette, <em|Kazhdan's Property (T)>,
  author manuscript, Theorem D.3.1, printed p.397, author URL
  <hlink|https://perso.univ-rennes1.fr/bachir.bekka/KazhdanTotal.pdf|https://perso.univ-rennes1.fr/bachir.bekka/KazhdanTotal.pdf>.
  The primary-source indexed page text was inspected and states the unique
  regular PVM theorem for a unitary representation of an LCA group. Direct
  PDF fetches timed out. This access limitation is not a claim of visual PDF
  inspection. The application is to the already proved strongly continuous
  representation of R4, with characters exp(i p.a). The Gaussian and measure
  transport arguments are additional proved steps, not attributed to SNAG.

  On 11 November the newly merged draft <verbatim|blueprint/background/osterwalder-schrader.md>
  (blob 2fc4e4096a102d182b1bca34d84eb191227be234, PR27; Trishen Gunaratnam
  with Codex assistance) was read. Its exact corrected OS-II
  E0\<prime\>/E0\<dprime\> growth quantifiers confirm why fixed-arity
  estimates alone do not justify invoking the general reconstruction theorem.
  Its documented C01\UC04/Shift direct route matches the chapters here. This
  is corroborating draft navigation, not an accepted reference proof or a
  claim of checking all its original scans. The new
  <verbatim|blueprint/interfaces/gaussian-sector.md> (blob
  9378ceea6c7112d3dab5d775fefbf1f5b6795fea, PR28) was read and passed to the
  estimate authors. It distinguishes the windowed covariance, full inverse,
  Haar normalization and relative logdet; its corrected exact hypotheses are
  retained as navigation for subsequent producer work. The independent
  reviewer rechecked its corrected Agreements.exact and Priced.chains
  paragraphs against their Lean source; no full-note or human acceptance is
  inferred.

  <section|Full tube and locality: the source's complete continuation
  route><label|full-tube-and-locality-the-sources-complete-continuation-route>

  <verbatim|full-tube.tex> follows <verbatim|YM.Work.C10>\U<verbatim|C16> in
  order: the suffix-cone pairing telescopes, a strict interior ball yields
  the dual margin, convolution of an indicator thickening gives the smooth
  cutoff, bounded closed shifts act continuously on Schwartz tests, and the
  strict lens has an exponential reserve.
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C13.hasFDerivAt_shift> and its <verbatim|Variation.lean>
  Taylor estimate give joint complex differentiation. C14's
  modulation-to-translation bound and compact Schwartz quadrature identify
  the integral, C15's compact negatively lifted tests and support identify
  the original strict-time wave, and C16 compares cutoffs only near the
  spectral cone for Lorentz covariance. The chapter proves each of these
  steps; it does not substitute a general reconstruction theorem.

  <verbatim|locality.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|YM.Work.C17>\U<verbatim|C21>, <verbatim|C27>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Shift/Swap.lean> and <verbatim|Exchange.lean>. Exact main
  declarations are C17.local_paths/height_path/answer;
  C18.eq_exponential/entire/answer; C19.paneAlong/answer;
  C20.jets_on_open_side/complex_germ/answer; C21.realize/reindex/answer;
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.Pane.agree>, <verbatim|propagate>;
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.NearPair.Panes.reaches>, <verbatim|forgets>,
  <verbatim|actor>; and C27.exchange/answer. The proof preserves the two
  uniform imaginary-boost paths, entire finite-level labels, two
  tube-anchored germs, equality of all Wick-slice jets, clopen germ
  propagation along real-time contraction, local dominated convergence,
  partial height removal, and product-test support argument. All spectators
  remain in the joint distributions. Finite-level inclusions and actual
  symmetry/calibration inputs are still required from the construction
  chapters.

  Independent gpt-6-astra review passed these chapters at the fingerprints
  recorded in reviews/draft-review.md, including source-main-step fidelity.
  This is agent review evidence, not accepted or kernel-verified mathematical
  status.

  <section|Finite-level Lorentz descent><label|finite-level-lorentz-descent>

  <verbatim|label-descent.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/A17.lean> and <verbatim|Lean/YM/Spin/Floor.lean>, at
  the recorded source pin. It proves the conjugated generator identity,
  differentiates Euclidean inclusion compatibility, uses constant-coefficient
  ODE uniqueness for boosts, then A16 generation to descend the actions to
  the field union. It deliberately does not assume the calibration maps
  commute with inclusions. Actual calibration and reference actions remain
  explicit inputs. Independent review passed fingerprint
  894d899b2dc2b222c1fe52b850131c92bcb3657264fffe5a919322099fb6cb69.

